# SUCCESS CRITERIA

Do not call the system production-ready merely because one metric is positive.

Before a model may advance toward the sealed exam, require evidence such as:

* meaningful improvement in probabilistic scoring versus incumbent;
* positive incremental cross-sectional information versus B3;
* directional performance better than trivial always-up baseline;
* confidence calibration behaving sensibly;
* high-confidence predictions materially stronger than low-confidence predictions;
* adequate coverage;
* adequate symbol breadth;
* no catastrophic regime inversion;
* uncertainty compatible with the claimed edge.

Set exact numerical thresholds using the existing research charter where already defined.

Where no threshold exists, derive a defensible threshold from sample size/power and **freeze it before evaluating candidate results**.

